  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb ({紡|つむ}ぐ → {紡|つむ}ぎます). Transitive.\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 2 has become very popular in modern Japanese, frequently appearing in book titles, song lyrics, and poetic prose. It conveys the idea of carefully and lovingly creating something over time, thread by thread.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {糸|いと}を{紡|つむ}ぐ: to spin thread\n- {言葉|ことば}を{紡|つむ}ぐ: to weave words\n- {物語|ものがたり}を{紡|つむ}ぐ: to weave a story\n- {絆|きずな}を{紡|つむ}ぐ: to build bonds\n- {歴史|れきし}を{紡|つむ}ぐ: to weave history",
